"><code>systemMessage</code></td><td style="text-align:left">none</td><td style="text-align:left">Warning message shown to the user. In <a class="link" href="/docs/en/agent-sdk/overview">Agent SDK</a> and <a class="link" href="/docs/en/headless"><code>--output-format stream-json</code></a> output, it can arrive as an <a class="link" href="/docs/en/agent-sdk/typescript#sdkinformationalmessage"><code>SDKInformationalMessage</code></a></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left"><code>terminalSequence</code></td><td style="text-align:left">none</td><td style="text-align:left">A terminal escape sequence for Claude Code to emit on your behalf, such as a desktop notification, window title, or bell. Restricted to OSC <code>0</code>/<code>1</code>/<code>2</code>/<code>9</code>/<code>99</code>/<code>777</code> and BEL. If the value contains anything outside the allowlist, the field is ignored. Use this instead of writing to <code>/dev/tty</code>, which is unavailable to hooks</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div></div>
<span data-as="p">To stop Claude entirely:</span>
