<span data-as="p">Runs when <a class="link" href="/docs/en/permission-modes#eliminate-prompts-with-auto-mode">auto mode</a> denies a tool call, including when it denies without a classifier verdict because <a class="link" href="/docs/en/errors#auto-mode-cannot-determine-the-safety-of-an-action">a safety check separate from auto mode refused the classifier’s own request</a> or its response didn’t parse. This hook only fires in auto mode: it doesn’t run when you manually deny a permission dialog, when a <code>PreToolUse</code> hook blocks a call, or when a <code>deny</code> rule matches. Use it to log denials, adjust configuration, or tell the model it may retry the tool call.</span>
<span data-as="p">Matches on tool name, same values as PreToolUse.</span>
