<span data-as="p">Runs when a configuration file changes during a session. Use this to audit settings changes, enforce security policies, or block unauthorized modifications to configuration files.</span>
<span data-as="p">Claude Code runs ConfigChange hooks when a settings file, a managed policy file, or a skill file changes. For managed policy, it runs them only when <code>managed-settings.json</code> or a file in <code>managed-settings.d/</code> changes. It applies <a class="link" href="/docs/en/server-managed-settings">server-managed settings</a> and changes to macOS managed preferences or Windows registry policy without running them. On WSL with <a class="link" href="/docs/en/settings-reference#wslinheritswindowssettings"><code>wslInheritsWindowsSettings</code></a>, it also applies a changed Windows-side managed settings file on its policy poll without running them.</span>
