<span data-as="p">The hook reads the changed file’s absolute path from the <code>file_path</code> field of the <a href="#filechanged-input" class="link">JSON input</a> on stdin. Its <code>grep</code> guard tests for the same thing <code>perl</code> removes, a CR at the end of a line, so the run after a normalization exits without touching the file. A looser guard loops forever, because <code>perl -i</code> rewrites the file even when it substitutes nothing and Claude Code runs the hook again after every rewrite. Save this script at <code>/path/to/normalize-line-endings.sh</code> and make it executable:</span>
