<span data-as="p">Async hooks have additional constraints compared to synchronous hooks:</span>
<ul>
<li>Hook output is delivered on the next conversation turn. If the session is idle, the response waits until the next user interaction. Exception: an <code>asyncRewake</code> hook that exits with code 2 wakes Claude immediately even when the session is idle.</li>
<li>Each execution creates a separate background process. There is no deduplication across multiple firings of the same async hook.</li>
</ul>
