rolling terminal. The hook process and any child processes can’t open `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`/dev/tty`}),` or send escape sequences directly to the Claude Code interface. Windows has no `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`/dev/tty`}),`.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`To surface a message to the user on any platform, return `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`#json-output`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`systemMessage`})}),` in JSON output. Some events discard it or deliver it elsewhere, and each `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`#hook-events`,children:`event’s section`}),` says so. To trigger a desktop notification, set a window title, or ring the bell, return `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`#emit-terminal-notifications`,children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`terminalSequence`})}),` instead.`]}),`\n`,_jsx(Heading,{level:`3`,id:`common-input-fields`,children:`Common input fields`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`Hook events receive these fields as JSON, in addition to event-specific fields documented in each `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`#hook-events`,children:`hook event`}),` section. For command hooks, this JSON arrives via stdin. For HTTP hooks, it arrives as the POST request body.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(Table,{children:[_jsx(_components.thead,{children:_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.th,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:`Field`}),_jsx(_components.th,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:`Description`})]})}),_jsxs(_components.tbody,{children:[_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`session_id`})}),_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:`Current session identifier`})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:_jsx(_components.code,{children:`prompt_id`})}),_jsxs(_components.td,{style:{textAlign:`left`},children:[`UUID identifying the user prompt currently being processed. Matches the `,_jsxs(_compo